Model weight tensors
--------------------
  One weight tensor derived from a third-party model checkpoint is committed
  as test data:

      testdata/rtl/a3_hc_pre_t1_checkpoint/projection.hex

  It is 393,216 F32 values of tensor `layers.0.hc_attn_fn` from
  deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731 at revision
  7872f01b1d1fe23eabc4c98b48bffcef5a386062, serialised as hex words. The
  sibling index.json records the checkpoint repository, revision and per-shard
  SHA-256 digests it was taken from.

  This tensor remains the property of its original authors and is governed by
  the DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731 model licence, NOT by OpenTallas' MIT licence.
  It is present so that one RTL campaign can be replayed bit-exactly against
  real checkpoint operands rather than synthetic data.

  Downstream users who cannot accept that licence should delete the file and
  regenerate it from their own copy of the checkpoint; the campaign that binds
  it will then need re-taking. If the upstream licence is found to prohibit
  redistribution of weight data, the correct remedy is removal, not this
  notice -- see docs/REPRODUCIBILITY.md for the boundary this repository
  claims.

  Model identities referenced by configuration (not redistributed): Qwen/Qwen3-8B,
  deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731, deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813,
  moonshotai/Kimi-K3. Their weights are NOT included; tooling fetches them
  from their upstream sources under their own licences.


